        "2": {
            "ID": "337921",
            "URL": "https://thetvdb.com/series/mega-man-star-force/seasons/official/2",
            "Titles": {
                "eng": "Ryuusei no Rockman: Tribe",
                "jpn": "流星のロックマン トライブ"
            },
            "Summaries": {
                "eng": "The ancient civilization of Mu vanished ages ago, and a few of its remnants still exist as myths and legends called UMAs (Unidentified Mystery Animals). The UMAs begin merging with humans in order to search for the treasures of Mu, the powerful OOPArts, which will give them the power to revive Mu. After Geo and Omega-Xis encounter several unusual enemies, they meet a professor named Doctor Vega who sends them on a quest to find the OOPArts and stop the UMAs.",
                "jpn": "人類が現在の文明を築き上げる、はるかかなた昔――\r\n地球には、知られざる文明ムーが栄華を誇っていたという。 ムーの人々は高い科学力を持ち、電波を自在に操る力で世界を支配していた。頂点を極めたムーの超科学は『究極の電波生命体』を造りだすまでになった。 だが『究極の電波生命体』の力はあまりにも大きく、神として人々に君臨しようとするに至る。ムー人はその力を恐れ、『究極の電波生命体』をムー大陸とともに封印してしまった。\r\nこうしてムー文明は地球上から姿を消し、今では世界各地に伝説や神話、ＵＭＡ（未確認生命体）の形でその片鱗が残されるのみとなっている。 そして……物語は、ＦＭ王ケフェウスが地球を訪れた時から始まっていた。ＦＭ王の巨大なエネルギーに反応し、ムー大陸の封印に綻びが生じてしまったのだ。目覚めかけた『究極の電波生命体』は、地球に生き残っていた電波生命体に呼び掛けた。\r\n「世界に散らばったムーの秘宝『オーパーツ』を捜しだせ！」とムーの電波生命体たちは活動を開始した。オーパーツ探索のため、電波変換可能な人間を探し出し、世界各地で事件を起こし始めたのだ。\r\nオーパーツのひとつ、『ベルセルク』を手に入れた星河スバルとウォーロックは、ムーの古代文明をめぐる争いに否応無く巻き込まれていく。 『オーパーツ』が集まった時、一体何が起きるのか。\r\n超古代文明ムーの謎を解くべく、ロックマンの新たなる冒険が始まった――！！"
            },
            "# Episodes": 21,
            "Episodes": {
                "1": {
                    "ID": "2993331",
                    "TYPE": null,
                    "URL": "https://www.thetvdb.com/series/mega-man-star-force/episodes/2993331",
                    "Titles": {
                        "eng": "The Inheritance of Mu",
                        "jpn": "ムーの遺産"
                    },
                    "Summaries": {
                        "eng": "A new breed of radio wave viruses have substantiated at a museum, so Subaru investigates. While there, he notices a strange aura emitting from a display item called the \"Sword of Berserk.\" Soon after, two new enemies appear  and begin to battle one another for the sword. In the heat of the struggle to protect the sword, War-Rock accidentally ingests it, and the enemies flee.",
                        "jpn": ""
                    },
                    "Aliases": []
                },
                "2": {
                    "ID": "2993341",
                    "TYPE": null,
                    "URL": "https://www.thetvdb.com/series/mega-man-star-force/episodes/2993341",
                    "Titles": {
                        "eng": "The Seal of Mu",
                        "jpn": "ムーの封印"
                    },
                    "Summaries": {
                        "eng": "After discussing the incident with Misora, Subaru meets a professor named Orihime. She explains that Cepheus's activity on Earth recently awakened the EM wave residents (UMAs) of the lost continent Mu. Mu was sealed with an extremely powerful EM wave being within it, and the UMAs wish to break the seal in order to release the being. But to do so, they require three ooparts—one of which is the sword stuck in War-Rock's stomach—and Orihime hopes to cooperate with Subaru in order to retrieve the ooparts first. Suddenly however, a mysterious new enemy named Burai attacks the university and assaults Subaru...",
                        "jpn": ""
                    },
                    "Aliases": []
                },
                "3": {
                    "ID": "2993351",
                    "TYPE": null,
                    "URL": "https://www.thetvdb.com/series/mega-man-star-force/episodes/2993351",
                    "Titles": {
                        "eng": "Burai's Attack",
                        "jpn": "ブライの襲撃"
                    },
                    "Summaries": {
                        "eng": "Rockman and Burai battle, but Burai is eventually forced to retreat after Orihime intervenes with a large jamming beam that disrupts EM wave activity. Later, Subaru takes War-Rock to AMAKEN to have the sword extracted from his stomach, and in the meantime, he and his friends play a materialization hammer game using the Star Carriers",
                        "jpn": ""
                    },
                    "Aliases": []
                },
                "4": {
                    "ID": "2993361",
                    "TYPE": null,
                    "URL": "https://www.thetvdb.com/series/mega-man-star-force/episodes/2993361",
                    "Titles": {
                        "eng": "Come Forth, Sword of Berserk!",
                        "jpn": "発動、ベルセルクの剣!"
                    },
                    "Summaries": {
                        "eng": "Subaru explains the quest for the ooparts to Misora, who expresses interest in helping. Burai attacks again, and the duo transform into Rockman and Harp Note to fight. Burai attempts to take the Sword of Berserk, but Rockman suddenly uses it to transform into the Thunder Berserk form, and defeats him.",
                        "jpn": ""
                    },
                    "Aliases": []
                },
                "5": {
                    "ID": "2993371",
                    "TYPE": null,
                    "URL": "https://www.thetvdb.com/series/mega-man-star-force/episodes/2993371",
                    "Titles": {
                        "eng": "The Yeti of the Himanalas",
                        "jpn": "ヒマナラの雪男"
                    },
                    "Summaries": {
                        "eng": "Orihime sends Subaru to the snowy mountain range of Himanala to locate an oopart. There, he meets a village girl named Lana who assists him in his search. She also tells of a yeti that has been terrorizing the village recently. Upon further investigation, Subaru encounters Yeti Blizzard, but he escapes amidst their battle.",
                        "jpn": ""
                    },
                    "Aliases": []
                },
                "6": {
                    "ID": "2993381",
                    "TYPE": null,
                    "URL": "https://www.thetvdb.com/series/mega-man-star-force/episodes/2993381",
                    "Titles": {
                        "eng": "The Mu Ruins of the Himanalas",
                        "jpn": "ヒマナラのムー遺跡"
                    },
                    "Summaries": {
                        "eng": "Rockman's quest for the oopart deepens as he begins to explore the ruins in the Himanalas. Yeti Blizzard tails him, hoping to swipe the treasure for himself, and Harp Note also appears to aid Rockman. In the end, there was no treasure, and Yeti Blizzard is defeated in an inevitable confrontation with the heroes.",
                        "jpn": ""
                    },
                    "Aliases": []
                },
                "7": {
                    "ID": "2993391",
                    "TYPE": null,
                    "URL": "https://www.thetvdb.com/series/mega-man-star-force/episodes/2993391",
                    "Titles": {
                        "eng": "Hyde and Ghost",
                        "jpn": "ハイドとゴースト"
                    },
                    "Summaries": {
                        "eng": "Subaru receives word from Orihime of an oopart hidden in a pyramid. Meanwhile, a painter named Hyde recalls when he first met his UMA partner, Ghost. Together, they are also traveling to the pyramid. Rockman explores the pyramid with hesitation, but eventually meets Hyde inside. Hyde transforms into Phantom Black, and Rockman counters with Thunder Berserker, but the sword is out of control!",
                        "jpn": ""
                    },
                    "Aliases": []
                },
                "8": {
                    "ID": "2993401",
                    "TYPE": null,
                    "URL": "https://www.thetvdb.com/series/mega-man-star-force/episodes/2993401",
                    "Titles": {
                        "eng": "Sword of Trials",
                        "jpn": "試しの剣"
                    },
                    "Summaries": {
                        "eng": "The sword causes Subaru to retreat, allowing Phantom Black to peacefully investigate the pyramid alone. To make matters worse, Burai soon appears and knocks Rockman unconscious. Within Subaru's psyche, he encounters the sword thrust into the ground. In an allusion to The Sword in the Stone, Subaru is able to pull the sword from the ground, awaken, and take control the Thunder Berserk form to defeat Burai. Meanwhile, Phantom Black finds that, unfortunately, the pyramid holds no treasure.",
                        "jpn": ""
                    },
                    "Aliases": []
                },
                "9": {
                    "ID": "2993411",
                    "TYPE": null,
                    "URL": "https://www.thetvdb.com/series/mega-man-star-force/episodes/2993411",
                    "Titles": {
                        "eng": "The Truth about Dossy",
                        "jpn": "ドッシーの真相"
                    },
                    "Summaries": {
                        "eng": "There's been a lot of buzz at Dombra Village about a lake beast nicknamed Dossy (a parody of Nessie), so Subaru travels there out of curiosity. He encounters a television director named Gerry Romero who is secretly gathering data on the beast. Furthermore, he runs into Monjirou Gori (the partner of UMA Yeti). Gerry is eventually pursued by a UMA and transforms into Plesio Surf, defeating both Yeti Blizzard and Rockman before retreating.",
                        "jpn": ""
                    },
                    "Aliases": []
                },
                "10": {
                    "ID": "2993421",
                    "TYPE": null,
                    "URL": "https://www.thetvdb.com/series/mega-man-star-force/episodes/2993421",
                    "Titles": {
                        "eng": "Brachio's Wish",
                        "jpn": "ブラキオの願い"
                    },
                    "Summaries": {
                        "eng": "Subaru and Misora discuss recent events when they meet the UMA Brachio. Brachio has been trying to protect the lake from intruders and pollution, and he had attacked Rockman in error. However, Gori commands a group of workers to begin filling in the lake, enraging  Brachio Wave and causing him to attack them. Rockman and Harp Note intervene, giving Gori the opportunity to submerge to the lake's bottom and steal the oopart hidden below.",
                        "jpn": ""
                    },
                    "Aliases": []
                },
